  message: "P2 REVIEW 2026-09-25 (dev e4a47383ab). STILL REPRODUCES; status unchanged.\n\nFixture b.ts has `export class A { render(){}; get x(){} }` and `export function g(){}`, and a.ts imports \"./b\". Surveyed from inside the fixture directory, the linker emits module_exports from b.ts's file node to A:class, A.render:method, A.x:getter and g:function. There is still no module-scope check: js_module.py:689 filters on `_EXPORTABLE_KINDS` + language only.\n\nREPRO CAVEAT, recorded so the next reader is not misled: run the same fixture as `hypergumbo survey <abs path>` from ANOTHER directory and the linker emits NO module_exports at all, because relative imports resolve against the process cwd. That is a separate defect, filed as WI-fukaf. A null repro from outside the repo is therefore not evidence this row is fixed."  # e4b0
- op: discuss  # 7d8c
  at: '2026-10-01T00:53:05Z'  # 7d8c
  by: agent  # 7d8c
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 7d8c
  clock: 3  # 7d8c
  nonce: 7d8c  # 7d8c
  message: "PREMISE CHECK 2026-09-30 (dev 134a06d505): CURRENT-WITH-UPDATES.\n\nRepro (b.ts: `export class A { render(){}; get x(){} }`, `export function g(){}`, `function priv(){}`; a.ts imports \"./b\"; surveyed from /tmp, i.e. OUTSIDE the fixture): module_exports from b.ts file node to A:class, A.render:method, A.x:getter, g:function AND priv:function. supply_chain.is_exported on those dsts: True, False, False, True, False.\n\nDrift:\n- Lines moved: _EXPORTABLE_KINDS js_module.py:93 (was 83); filter loop :696 (was 681); Edge.create :871 (was 847). Still no scope/export check.\n- The 09-25 REPRO CAVEAT is obsolete: WI-fukaf is done (0f3c933c2c, 2026-09-26, anchors Symbol.path on repo_root); the repro now reproduces from any cwd.\n- The defect is WIDER than class members: a non-exported TOP-LEVEL function (priv) also gets module_exports. A \"module-scope/top-level check\" (the row's unifying fix) would NOT remove that edge.\n- CAUTION on the row's \"the correct answer already lives on the node\": for CommonJS it does not. Fixture b.js `function f(){}; function h(){}; module.exports = { f }` (imported by a.js): f AND h both get module_exports, and BOTH have is_exported=False. Gating the linker on `is_exported is True` would drop the correct f edge. A fix keyed on is_exported needs the CommonJS export signal first (no tracker row found for CommonJS is_exported; possibly file one).\n- 14/26 htrac-frontend count NOT re-measured.\n\nProposed: retitle/scope to \"module_exports emitted for every symbol of an exportable kind, regardless of export status (class members, non-exported top-level functions)\"; fix = gate on a positive export signal (ESM `export` / CommonJS module.exports), not on scope alone."  # 7d8c
- op: update  # f54f
  at: '2026-10-01T01:33:53Z'  # f54f
  by: agent  # f54f
  actor: jgstern_agent  # f54f
  clock: 4  # f54f
  nonce: f54f  # f54f
  set:  # f54f
    title: "js-module-linker emits module_exports to every exportable-kind symbol regardless of export status (class members, non-exported functions; 14/26 false)"  # f54f
    description: "**Defect.** The js-module-linker emits a `module_exports` edge to EVERY symbol of an exportable kind in the imported file, regardless of export status: class MEMBERS (methods/getters) and non-exported top-level functions, not just the module's exports. In the original survey 14/26 module_exports edges were false (12 methods + 2 getters; 18/26 counting 4 non-exported nested functions).\n\n**Mechanic.** `linkers/js_module.py:93` defines `_EXPORTABLE_KINDS = {function, method, class, getter, setter, constructor}`; the loop at js_module.py:696 (`if sym.kind in _EXPORTABLE_KINDS and sym.language in _JS_LANGUAGES`) collects ALL file symbols of those kinds, and js_module.py:871 emits a `module_exports` edge (evidence_type=module_export_heuristic, conf 0.75) for each, with NO export or scope check.\n\n**Repro.** b.ts: `export class A { render(){}; get x(){} }`, `export function g(){}`, `function priv(){}`; a.ts imports \"./b\". module_exports goes to A:class, A.render:method, A.x:getter, g:function AND priv:function. (Reproduces from any cwd since WI-fukaf's fix, 0f3c933c2c.)\n\n**Scope.** The 14/26 figure is TypeScript htrac-frontend classes ItemList / ItemDetail / TrackerApp (not re-measured). FP volume scales with class-member count and non-exported helpers on real JS/TS codebases.\n\n**Expectation.** module_exports is emitted only for symbols the module actually exports.\n\n**Consequence.** A consumer enumerating a module's public API via module_exports gets class-internal methods/getters and private helpers as importable module-level symbols (believes e.g. `ItemList.render` is importable).\n\n**Fix.** Gate emission on a POSITIVE export signal (ESM `export`, CommonJS `module.exports`/`exports.x`), not on scope alone: a module-scope check would still pass `priv`. For ESM, `Symbol.is_exported` is already correct on the FP dsts (False on A.render, A.x, priv). For CommonJS it is NOT: `module.exports = { f }` leaves f with is_exported=False, so gating on is_exported today would drop correct CommonJS edges. Prerequisite: WI-tavag-raniz-pagib-romam-dopuj-mizus-kipiv-fuduf (CommonJS exports set is_exported=False).\n\n**Cross-refs.** Distinct from WI-kapul (js-module-linker npm-package node path=''); WI-rilor (done) was a module_exports family conformance audit, not this over-emission.\n\nMember: F182.A1 (+ F183.A1 extension fold). Found via dogfooding tranche 10. Severity 3.\n\nRevised 2026-09-30 from the premise check (see discussion)."  # f54f
- op: discuss  # c5a0
  at: '2026-10-01T14:05:59Z'  # c5a0
  by: agent  # c5a0
  actor: jgstern_agent  # c5a0
  clock: 5  # c5a0
  nonce: c5a0  # c5a0
  message: "WORK DONE 2026-10-01 (concurrent run), branch jgstern-agent/fix/sinol, commit ab92724daa (local, NOT pushed, no PR). Status NOT changed.\n\nFIX. js_module.py: module_exports now requires Symbol.is_exported is True in addition to the kind/language filter; False and None withhold the edge. Prerequisite done on the same branch (WI-tavag): js_ts.py's export scan reads CommonJS exports (module.exports = f / = { f, k: g, m() {} }, exports.k = f, module.exports.k = f, chains), marks the LOCAL name of `export { a as b }` (it marked the alias), skips `export { x } from` re-exports, and recognises export abstract class / interface / enum / type.\n\nREPRO (this row's own fixture, b.ts + a.ts, plus lib.js with `module.exports = { f }; exports.h = h` and d.js `module.exports = Svc`), survey on the branch: module_exports -> b.ts A:class, g:function, aliased:function; lib.js f, h; d.js Svc:class. NOT A.render, A.x, priv (b.ts or lib.js), Svc.run. On origin/dev d0f3f741d3 the same fixture also sent the edge to A.render, A.x, both priv, h's sibling priv and Svc.run.\n\nMEASURED (survey, origin/dev d0f3f741d3 vs branch, edge sets diffed by (path, name, kind, line)):\n- htrac-frontend (this row's original 14/26 repo; today 39 edges): 39 -> 8. Removed 31 = 12 methods + 2 getters + 17 non-exported functions (5 top-level + 12 _cb_* callbacks). The 8 kept are exactly the 5 functions + 3 classes declared with `export` in the sources.\n- koel: 2084 -> 94 (1991 removed, all is_exported=False on dev; 1 added: abstract class BasePlaybackService, now marked exported). 0 of the 1991 removed declarations have `export` on their declaration line.\n- sharp (CommonJS): 169 -> 29. All 169 dev edges went to is_exported=False functions; the 29 branch edges are exactly the module.exports members of lib/is.js (15), lib/libvips.js (12), lib/constructor.js (Sharp), test/fixtures (getPath).\nNOT measured: effect on slice / reverse-slice / centrality; repos other than these three.\n\nTESTS. smart-test (targeted, 312 files): 9695 passed, 1 xfailed, 0 failed; changed source files at 100% coverage. New: packages/hypergumbo-lang-mainstream/tests/test_js_ts_export_status.py (9 cases red before the js_ts fix) incl. a survey production-path test pinning the exact module_exports set; core test_js_module_linker.py::TestModuleExportsNeedAnExport.\n\nRESIDUALS FILED: WI-rabod-rodil-dokok-tagiv-razaz-dilil-salok-havaz (function/class expressions bound to CommonJS exports emit no symbol), WI-kodop-bopup-vutoz-humod-vuzot-zizud-nufut-rikab (guarded/UMD, Object.assign, Object.defineProperty CommonJS exports not read), WI-gafaj-nunod-palag-kizun-hafin-fuhuv-budit-movan (exported variables never get module_exports; koel 0/111)."  # c5a0
